# M0 ACCEPTANCE (c). A class that is declared and otherwise unmentioned must still
# GET A CONTEXT, because the registry is keyed on the input SIGNATURE rather than on
# axiom occurrence. Otherwise HOWL cannot answer Unused subseteq top, cannot list it
# in a hierarchy, and cannot serve a probe naming it -- not an error, just a class
# the reasoner silently does not know exists.

@prefix :    <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class .
:A rdfs:subClassOf :B .
:Unused a owl:Class .
